Real-world example: E-commerce

Imagine Amazon-like system.
You have millions of orders:

Orders
   ↓
Complex aggregation
   ↓
Materialized View
   ↓
"Top 10 products sold today"

Instead of calculating this every time someone opens the dashboard:

SELECT product_id, COUNT(*)
FROM orders
GROUP BY product_id
ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC
LIMIT 10;

You precompute:

Materialized View

1. Nike Shoes       → 50,000 sold
2. Adidas Shoes     → 45,000 sold
3. Puma Shoes       → 40,000 sold

Dashboard reads directly from the materialized view.
